 "floorplan_note": "q2 identity2 --cts gate failed GPL-0305 (NaN) twice with the generated 3-macro column (20 um macro-macro channels, 5.4 um halos -> 9.5 um cell rows between arrays; overflow stuck at 0.115 for 12k iterations). Structural: the three arrays (pins only on W/E faces) form one abutted N-S stack (pitch = array height + 0.024 um) centred in the core, so no narrow inter-array channel exists; two ~70 um N/S channels carry the cross traffic.",
 "pg_layer": "M6",
 "layer_cap_grant": "H-DIE 2210 v4: VM bank strap masters are pin-perimeter bound (270 x 270, ~1,260 b per face): PG moves to M6 so M5 pins need no stripe clearance; parent strap M7 (H-DIE 2210, H-SM proposal)",
 "structural_change": "Native q2 failed L250.8/C194.4/spread46.9 despite routed timing. New master uses four literal face-local related roots plus core/SRAM root; existing boundary stages only, return7/writeDone4 preserved. Same270square/3 actual SRAMs. No default/compiler adoption. | faces-mclk A: the 3 SRAM clock pins move off core clk onto direct entries clk_macro0..2 (W face at each SRAM clk pin; hybrid_entries; CTS roots clk/clk_n/clk_s/clk_e/clk_w reach standard cells only). Abutted stack .024 um slivers hard-blocked (macro_channel_block). | faces-mclk B: the 3 SRAM clock pins move off core clk onto direct entries clk_macro0..2 (W face at each SRAM clk pin; hybrid_entries; CTS roots clk/clk_n/clk_s/clk_e/clk_w reach standard cells only). Outline 270x313.2 (+16%): 20.136 um macro channels.",
